1. Third-party model code (Apache-2.0)
================================================================================

FLUX.2 (Black Forest Labs)
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-base-4B

    a) Transformer primitives. src/reflowset/transformer_reflowset.py adapts
       SingleStreamBlock, DoubleStreamBlock, Modulation, QKNorm, RMSNorm,
       EmbedND / rope / apply_rope, MLPEmbedder and timestep_embedding from
       Black Forest Labs' FLUX.2 model code. MODIFIED: the text stream is
       replaced by a SAR stream, the conditioning path and the output head
       differ, and the training-only REPA projector is absent from this
       inference port.

    b) Autoencoder. src/reflowset/autoencoder_flux2.py is a port of the same
       upstream's autoencoder, used FROZEN and never fine-tuned. MODIFIED:
       re-expressed as a diffusers ModelMixin; the encoder returns the posterior
       mean and discards the log-variance; a 2x2 space-to-depth pack and the
       shipped BatchNorm latent normaliser are applied at the module boundary.

    The autoencoder WEIGHTS are redistributed with the checkpoints. They are the
    Apache-2.0 file from FLUX.2-klein-base-4B, re-serialised from diffusers key
    names to the upstream layout and cast to bfloat16. Tensors were paired BY
    VALUE, not by an assumed rename table; the round trip is bit-identical to
    the source through a full encode/decode. scripts/convert_flux2_ae.py plus
    assets/flux2_ae_key_map.json reproduce the file from the official download.

    SUBSTITUTED AFTER TRAINING, and stated plainly because it matters: both
    released arms were TRAINED and EVALUATED with the FLUX.2-dev serialisation
    of this autoencoder. That file encoded and decoded every image during
    training and during the evaluation that produced the paper's table. It is
    published under the FLUX Non-Commercial License, whose Section 4(a)(iii)
    forbids "surveillance purposes, including all research and development
    related to surveillance" and whose Section 1(a) makes the restriction
    inherit permanently.

    The file published here is the Apache-2.0 serialisation of the SAME network,
    from FLUX.2-klein-base-4B. 250 of 251 tensors pair one-to-one by value with
    a worst absolute deviation of 7.80e-03 (bfloat16 rounding; 3.89e-03
    relative), and the unpaired entry is a BatchNorm step counter rather than a
    weight. Swapping it into the released checkpoints, measured end to end,
    changes QXS-SAROPT PSNR by less than 0.004 dB in absolute value; four
    independent measurements at different guidance scales and sample sets land
    between -0.004 and +0.002 dB, so the sign is not resolved and only the
    magnitude is meaningful. For scale, changing only the evaluation seed moves
    the same measurement by +0.395 dB. Nothing the paper prints changes.

